      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "e481c21bb0d165da461286b282a55c17ce6b6d7611989a9501732a61237365fb",
      "skos:note": "Defines office under the Commonwealth"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/national-crime-authority-status-and-rights-of-former-chairman-act-1984#sec-3",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "3 Interpretation",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 5,
      "values:originalText": "In this Act:\noffice under the Commonwealth includes:\n\n(a) an office established by, or an appointment made under, a\nlaw of the Commonwealth or a law of a Territory other than\nthe Northern Territory;\n\n(b) an appointment made by the Governor-General or a Minister\notherwise than under such a law;\n\n(c) an office or appointment in the service or employment of a\ncorporation established for a public purpose by or under a\nlaw of the Commonwealth or a law of a Territory other than\nthe Northern Territory;\n\n(d) an appointment as a director of an incorporated company\nover which the Commonwealth is in a position to exercise\ncontrol; or\n\n(e) an office or appointment in the service or employment of\nsuch an incorporated company.\nremuneration includes any expenses of office allowance, annual\nallowance or other allowance in the nature of remuneration.\nretirement has the same meaning as in the Judges’ Pensions Act\n1968.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2011C00791\n\n\n\nSection 4"
    },
