    {
      "@id": "concept:national-crime-authority-status-and-rights-of-former-chairman-act-1984-sec-8",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "8 Application of Judges’ Pensions Act",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/national-crime-authority-status-and-rights-of-former-chairman-act-1984#sec-8"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "national-crime-authority-status-and-rights-of-former-chairman-act-1984.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "national-crime-authority-status-and-rights-of-former-chairman-act-1984.pdf, p.8",
      "values:originalText": "The application in relation to the Honourable Donald Gerard\nStewart of the Judges’ Pensions Act 1968 is subject to the\nfollowing provisions of this section:\n\n(a) service by him as Chairman of the National Crime Authority,\nwhether the service took place before, or takes place after,\nthe commencement of this Act, shall be deemed, for the\npurposes of the Judges’ Pensions Act 1968, to have been, or\nto be, service as a Judge;\n\n(aa) service by him as Chairperson of the Resource Assessment\nCommission shall be taken, for the purposes of the Judges’\nPensions Act 1968, to be service as a Judge;\n\n(b) upon his death or retirement, the appropriate current judicial\nsalary in relation to him for the purposes of the Judges’\nPensions Act 1968 shall be deemed to be the salary from time\nto time payable to a Judge of the Supreme Court of New\nSouth Wales;\n\n(c) for the purposes of paragraph 6(2D)(a) of the Judges’\nPensions Act 1968, he shall be deemed to be a judge who is\nto cease to hold office as a judge upon his attaining a\nparticular age being the age:\n\n(i) if subparagraph (ii) does not apply—that will be\nattained by him at the expiration of the period of his\nappointment as Chairperson of the Resource\nAssessment Commission; or\n\n(ii) in the event of his re-appointment as such\nChairperson—at the expiration of the period of such\nre-appointment.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2011C00791\n\n\n\nSection 9\n\nNational Crime Authority (Status and Rights of Former Chairman) Act 1984\n\n(d) if, during any period after his retirement, he holds, or\nperforms the duties of, a full-time office under the\nCommonwealth, pension is not payable to him under the\nJudges’ Pensions Act 1968 in respect of that period.",
      "skos:definition": "The application in relation to the Honourable Donald Gerard\nStewart of the Judges’ Pensions Act 1968 is subject to the\nfollowing provisions of this section:\n\n(a) service by him as Chairman of the National Crime Authority,\nwhether the service took place before, or takes place after,\nthe commencement of this Act, shall be deemed, for the\npurposes of the Judges’ Pensions Act 1968, to have been, or\nto be, service as a Judge;\n\n(aa) service by him as Chairperson of the Resource Assessment\nCommission shall be taken, for the purposes of the Judges’\nPensions Act 1968, to be service as a Judge;\n\n(b) upon his death or retirement, the appropriate current judicial\nsalary in relation to him for the purposes of the Judges’\nPensions Act 1968 shall be deemed to be the salary from time\nto time payable to a Judge of the Supreme Court of New\nSouth Wales;\n\n(c) for the purposes of paragraph 6(2D)(a) of the Judges’\nPensions Act 1968, he shall be deemed to be a judge who is\nto cease to hold office as a judge upon his attaining a\nparticular age being the age:\n\n(i) if subparagraph (ii) does not apply—that will be\nattained by him at the expiration of the period of his\nappointment as Chairperson of the Resource\nAssessment Commission; or\n\n(ii) in the event of his re-appointment as such\nChairperson—at the expiration of the period of such\nre-appointment.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2011C00791\n\n\n\nSection 9\n\nNational Crime Authority (Status and Rights of Former Chairman) Act 1984\n\n(d) if, during any period after his retirement, he holds, or\nperforms the duties of, a full-time office under the\nCommonwealth, pension is not payable to him under the\nJudges’ Pensions Act 1968 in respect of that period.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:national-crime-authority-status-and-rights-of-former-chairman-act-1984-sec-8-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:national-crime-authority-status-and-rights-of-former-chairman-act-1984-sec-8-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:national-crime-authority-status-and-rights-of-former-chairman-act-1984-sec-8-logic-alleninterval-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:national-crime-authority-status-and-rights-of-former-chairman-act-1984-sec-8-logic-linearlogic-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:national-crime-authority-status-and-rights-of-former-chairman-act-1984-sec-8-logic-dialectical-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:national-crime-authority-status-and-rights-of-former-chairman-act-1984-sec-8-logic-argumentation-5"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "78b91277312e127d532b9c5cb757d6efafd0f7aa50713900f2f0ff54a630c0b6",
      "skos:note": "Deems service as Chairman of National Crime Authority and Chairperson of Resource Assessment Commission as Judge's service for purposes of Judges' Pensions Act 1968."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/national-crime-authority-status-and-rights-of-former-chairman-act-1984#sec-8",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "8 Application of Judges’ Pensions Act",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 8,
      "values:originalText": "The application in relation to the Honourable Donald Gerard\nStewart of the Judges’ Pensions Act 1968 is subject to the\nfollowing provisions of this section:\n\n(a) service by him as Chairman of the National Crime Authority,\nwhether the service took place before, or takes place after,\nthe commencement of this Act, shall be deemed, for the\npurposes of the Judges’ Pensions Act 1968, to have been, or\nto be, service as a Judge;\n\n(aa) service by him as Chairperson of the Resource Assessment\nCommission shall be taken, for the purposes of the Judges’\nPensions Act 1968, to be service as a Judge;\n\n(b) upon his death or retirement, the appropriate current judicial\nsalary in relation to him for the purposes of the Judges’\nPensions Act 1968 shall be deemed to be the salary from time\nto time payable to a Judge of the Supreme Court of New\nSouth Wales;\n\n(c) for the purposes of paragraph 6(2D)(a) of the Judges’\nPensions Act 1968, he shall be deemed to be a judge who is\nto cease to hold office as a judge upon his attaining a\nparticular age being the age:\n\n(i) if subparagraph (ii) does not apply—that will be\nattained by him at the expiration of the period of his\nappointment as Chairperson of the Resource\nAssessment Commission; or\n\n(ii) in the event of his re-appointment as such\nChairperson—at the expiration of the period of such\nre-appointment.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2011C00791\n\n\n\nSection 9\n\nNational Crime Authority (Status and Rights of Former Chairman) Act 1984\n\n(d) if, during any period after his retirement, he holds, or\nperforms the duties of, a full-time office under the\nCommonwealth, pension is not payable to him under the\nJudges’ Pensions Act 1968 in respect of that period."
    },
